WEBVTT

00:10.800 --> 00:11.810
A girl?!

00:11.810 --> 00:14.560
Impossible! She's inside 
a glacier from the Ice Age!

00:21.060 --> 00:23.630
Contact the Arcane Court immediately!

00:23.630 --> 00:24.310
Yes, sir!

00:24.930 --> 00:27.180
Well, this isn't good.

00:27.770 --> 00:29.950
Has it been a thousand years? 
Two thousand?

00:32.310 --> 00:33.170
Could it be?

00:34.110 --> 00:35.470
I guess I might've overslept.

00:39.700 --> 00:42.150
Who are you?

00:42.550 --> 00:43.460
Me?

00:43.770 --> 00:45.490
I'm a former god.

00:45.910 --> 00:48.310
But that hardly matters.

00:49.420 --> 00:54.170
Bring me this era's very best player.

01:00.160 --> 01:03.510
This game is already on fire!

01:03.950 --> 01:05.800
The gods' games!

01:05.800 --> 01:08.400
What god will humanity 
be challenging today?

01:08.400 --> 01:10.200
There're actually three!

01:10.200 --> 01:11.840
There's never been a 
challenge like this before!

01:12.360 --> 01:16.090
<i>People from all over 
the world are watching the</i>

01:16.090 --> 01:18.760
<i>stream to see this 
historical moment take place!</i>

01:20.200 --> 01:25.170
<b>Ruin, the Sacrament City</b>

01:26.810 --> 01:28.630
Hey, are you watching today's stream?

01:28.630 --> 01:30.520
Yeah, totally! Why don't 
we watch it together?

01:30.520 --> 01:31.120
Sure!

01:40.530 --> 01:42.180
I guess it's been six months now.

01:44.840 --> 01:48.780
<i>A Salamander! It's letting lose 
one ring of fire after another!</i>

01:44.920 --> 01:46.240
The gods' games?

01:46.980 --> 01:48.780
They're doing three at once?

01:49.500 --> 01:51.670
<i>And the apostles are dodging each one!</i>

01:52.020 --> 01:55.660
<i>They're showing some excellent moves as they draw nearer to the Salamander!</i>

01:58.640 --> 02:02.620
<i>Uh oh! Looks like Team C 
activated a trap!</i>

02:03.890 --> 02:05.350
No!

02:07.530 --> 02:11.310
<i>Looks like the Salamander 
figured out their moves!</i>

02:11.310 --> 02:12.970
<i>And defeat!</i>

02:13.040 --> 02:18.520
<b> Defeat
VS Elemental Salamander
"Blazing Inferno Relay"
16 Apostles All Defeated</b>

02:21.930 --> 02:23.140
<b> VS Demon Nacht
"Reverse Tag"</b>

02:23.140 --> 02:24.510
<b>VS Demon Nacht
"Reverse Tag"
40 Apostles All Defeated</b>

02:24.510 --> 02:26.230
<b> Defeat
VS Demon Nacht
"Reverse Tag"
40 Apostles All Defeated</b>

02:27.730 --> 02:28.940
<b> VS The Endless God Uroboros
"?????"</b>

02:28.940 --> 02:29.980
<b>VS The Endless God Uroboros
"?????"
69 Apostles All Forfeited</b>

02:29.980 --> 02:32.200
<b>Defeat
VS The Endless God Uroboros
"?????"
69 Apostles All Forfeited</b>

02:38.130 --> 02:41.640
I guess I should get going. 
After all, I'm also a challenger.

02:42.590 --> 02:43.980
Isn't that Fay?

02:44.180 --> 02:45.310
He's back?

02:46.390 --> 02:48.370
<i>Fay's here? Where?</i>

02:48.370 --> 02:50.380
<i>Huh? Fay? </i>The<i> Fay?</i>

02:51.460 --> 02:54.300
Ruin Branch Office of the Arcane Court

03:00.180 --> 03:01.240
Hey, look.

03:02.150 --> 03:03.410
I-Is that Fay?

03:03.670 --> 03:04.930
I've never seen him before.

03:08.820 --> 03:11.630
Welcome back, Fay. I believe 
it's been about six months.

03:11.880 --> 03:13.310
Did you lose some weight?

03:13.800 --> 03:17.300
Yeah, a bit. More importantly, 
what's going on, Chief Secretary?!

03:18.580 --> 03:24.050
So apparently this girl you spent six months looking for turned out to be the wrong person?

03:24.050 --> 03:25.220
Yes.

03:25.220 --> 03:28.920
Didn't you say that you found 
someone who looked just like her?

03:29.350 --> 03:32.760
The girl I was looking for had bright red hair.

03:33.120 --> 03:36.270
The lady who taught you how to play games when you were younger, right?

03:36.650 --> 03:39.770
All I said was that I heard 
rumors of someone like that.

03:40.380 --> 03:41.390
But anyway...

03:41.690 --> 03:43.610
I need to speak with you.

03:44.030 --> 03:45.260
Come up to the 17th floor.

03:45.840 --> 03:47.210
About what?

03:47.670 --> 03:49.030
What else?

03:49.280 --> 03:52.540
We're going to talk about the game 
between humanity and the gods.

03:55.840 --> 03:58.090
There's a girl I'd like you to meet.

03:58.680 --> 04:02.140
She apparently said, "Bring me 
this era's very best player."

04:02.720 --> 04:05.250
And that's basically you, Fay.

04:05.630 --> 04:07.060
Who is this girl?

04:07.060 --> 04:08.140
A god.

04:09.970 --> 04:16.220
A year ago, a god in the form of a girl was dug out of some permafrost.

04:16.740 --> 04:22.520
Wasn't she taken into our Arcane 
Court because we were close by?

04:23.240 --> 04:25.320
She's definitely a strange one.

04:25.840 --> 04:30.240
She hid on the sea floor while 
playing tag with some humans.

04:30.890 --> 04:33.390
But while she was hiding...

04:34.480 --> 04:37.020
She fell asleep and 
headed right into the Ice Age.

04:37.020 --> 04:40.170
She accidentally napped for the last
 three thousand years, totally frozen.

04:40.490 --> 04:43.110
Can you really call that a nap?

04:43.610 --> 04:47.950
She's apparently an avatar of 
flame in the form of a dragon

04:48.600 --> 04:52.680
and says that she's a former god
 whose powers have declined.

04:52.680 --> 04:54.150
She's still pretty menacing though.

04:54.490 --> 04:55.260
What do you mean?

04:55.840 --> 04:57.280
We definitely shouldn't make her angry.

04:57.710 --> 05:01.380
Within an hour, this city would disappear off 
the world map and be reduced to ashes.

05:01.890 --> 05:06.090
So why are you holding onto 
such a dangerous god?

05:06.380 --> 05:09.450
Well, we didn't think she was 
that dangerous at first.

05:12.430 --> 05:13.330
Let's get down to business.

05:13.610 --> 05:16.550
You'll be watching over this god, Fay.

05:17.160 --> 05:17.800
Sorry, what?

05:19.780 --> 05:23.260
You want me to watch over a god?!

05:25.200 --> 05:28.460
Superior spiritual beings known 
as gods have descended to Earth...

05:29.090 --> 05:31.490
and we humans still don't know why.

05:33.360 --> 05:35.540
I'd like to know why she's still here.

05:35.950 --> 05:38.980
But if we get too nosey 
and make her mad...

05:38.980 --> 05:40.650
We'd all be in big trouble.

05:41.810 --> 05:43.940
That's why you're perfect for this job.

05:44.350 --> 05:46.170
Actually, you're the only 
one who can do this.

05:47.370 --> 05:48.780
Because I won't die?

05:49.250 --> 05:53.460
Correct. The power of the gods is just too 
great and can destroy humans easily.

05:53.880 --> 05:57.530
That's why we need to ask you to do this 
since you possess the Arise to not die.

06:00.150 --> 06:02.190
She chose you herself.

06:03.970 --> 06:07.400
Well, you're going to have to 
put on a little show, but...

06:07.820 --> 06:10.490
Don't worry. You won't be going it alone.

06:15.310 --> 06:16.180
Huh...

06:16.910 --> 06:19.730
<i>I guess this god must truly love games.</i>

06:27.440 --> 06:28.430
Four and six.

06:32.280 --> 06:33.730
Wait, was that a coincidence?

06:33.730 --> 06:34.870
It's easy.

06:35.120 --> 06:37.500
Make sure the opposite side 
of the desired numbers are facing up.

06:39.280 --> 06:43.300
Then throw them with enough 
force to make them do a half turn.

06:43.570 --> 06:44.880
Oh, Miranda.

06:56.540 --> 06:59.860
Hey, Miranda. Is that human...

07:00.220 --> 07:04.390
This is this era's very best 
player that you've been asking for.

07:04.840 --> 07:08.610
Ever since he debuted last year, 
he's won three gods' games.

07:08.610 --> 07:10.360
He's an apostle that's the top of the line.

07:10.800 --> 07:13.930
This is Fay. He's been assigned here 
as a supervisor starting today.

07:14.520 --> 07:18.160
This is Lady Leoleshea. Say hello.

07:18.790 --> 07:19.480
Hmm?

07:19.480 --> 07:21.340
She just happens to look like her, right?

07:22.020 --> 07:23.960
Earth to Fay.

07:25.720 --> 07:27.630
Is something the matter, human?

07:29.310 --> 07:31.620
Anyway, I gotta get back to work,

07:31.620 --> 07:34.350
so you two can introduce yourselves 
and get to know each other better.

07:34.870 --> 07:38.950
Fay, don't mess up this supervisor role.

07:42.950 --> 07:44.630
Uh, um...

07:45.390 --> 07:46.690
Lady Leoleshea?

07:50.500 --> 07:52.260
Well, let's get started.

07:52.530 --> 07:54.720
You and I are going to play a game.

07:55.470 --> 07:58.400
Before that, why don't we introduce ourselves?

07:58.810 --> 08:02.160
Since I'll be a supervisor, I was hoping 
we could get to know each other...

08:02.160 --> 08:04.970
We're going to be introducing 
ourselves through this game.

08:08.020 --> 08:10.890
<i>This isn't a gods' game...</i>

08:11.640 --> 08:12.800
<i>is it?</i>

08:13.540 --> 08:15.680
<i>We're not in an Elements either.</i>

08:15.680 --> 08:17.140
Hmm? What is it?

08:17.650 --> 08:18.880
Err, nothing...

08:20.680 --> 08:25.660
Name, age, hometown, hobbies, dreams...

08:26.400 --> 08:28.050
I made these when I got bored.

08:28.860 --> 08:31.820
I call it Self-Intro Memory.

08:32.560 --> 08:34.780
That name's pretty straightforward.

08:34.950 --> 08:37.660
The rules are the same as a regular game of Memory.

08:37.660 --> 08:40.440
But you won't be pairing with numbers.

08:40.440 --> 08:42.260
You'll be pairing with the 
subject and theme of the self-intro.

08:45.190 --> 08:50.560
For example, if I happen to match "hometown," 
you'll answer with your hometown.

08:48.360 --> 08:53.660
<b>Hometown</b>

08:51.090 --> 08:53.670
If I don't get a match, you don't need to answer.

08:53.880 --> 08:54.730
Understood.

08:56.730 --> 09:00.910
Just answer truthfully to 
whatever the matched pair says.

09:01.150 --> 09:02.070
Of course.

09:03.120 --> 09:04.240
Oh, one sec.

09:04.780 --> 09:07.510
Could you reshuffle those cards?

09:08.260 --> 09:11.020
When you lined them up on the table, 
you had them all facing up, didn't you?

09:11.400 --> 09:13.240
To explain the rules to me.

09:13.940 --> 09:17.370
You memorized the locations 
of all the cards that quickly

09:17.850 --> 09:20.200
and then saw how they all shuffled?

09:20.440 --> 09:21.370
It's a habit of mine.

09:21.680 --> 09:25.160
A certain person almost trained me 
to death on how to play games.

09:25.810 --> 09:28.480
Nice. I like you.

09:29.490 --> 09:32.790
Especially the fact that you didn't want 
to use a cheat where you memorized

09:32.790 --> 09:35.590
all the cards and want to play 
against a god fair and square.

09:36.580 --> 09:41.450
In that case, maybe we shouldn't play 
this game on such a small table.

09:43.420 --> 09:46.790
Float and begin turning.

09:52.380 --> 09:55.420
Are they all moving at 
different orbits and speeds?

09:55.820 --> 09:57.700
Ah, so you've already noticed.

09:58.360 --> 10:02.760
Each card has a different orbit, so I don't 
know how they're going to turn either.

10:03.520 --> 10:05.400
This seems more fun, doesn't it?

10:06.070 --> 10:09.720
So we're playing a game of 3D Memory...

10:10.360 --> 10:13.830
<i>Once we reveal a card, I won't forget its location...</i>

10:14.250 --> 10:16.020
<i>and neither will she.</i>

10:16.420 --> 10:21.000
<i>So she basically added on a rule that'll 
continuously keep changing the cards' locations.</i>

10:21.520 --> 10:23.390
Oh, one last thing.

10:24.180 --> 10:26.190
I want to add a unique rule.

10:26.590 --> 10:27.750
What kind of rule?

10:28.260 --> 10:30.230
The "Absolutely One Turn Only" rule.

10:31.200 --> 10:36.490
<i>In a regular game of Memory, you get a 
matching pair, you get another turn, right?</i>

10:37.240 --> 10:38.950
That's not going to happen in this game.

10:39.240 --> 10:40.460
I see.

10:40.900 --> 10:45.910
<i>Out of all games, that added rule
 is going to be a pain.</i>

10:46.410 --> 10:49.780
<i>Which means this is no longer
 just a game of memorization.</i>

10:53.460 --> 10:55.210
Okay, let the game start!

10:55.900 --> 10:57.300
I'm ready when you are.

11:04.480 --> 11:06.390
Looks like it's begun.

11:10.590 --> 11:11.890
Okay, let's begin.

11:12.510 --> 11:14.530
You can have the first turn.

11:15.030 --> 11:18.740
If you insist. I'll take those two.

11:22.620 --> 11:25.830
Huh... Hometown and blood type.

11:23.300 --> 11:26.110
Blood type                                                                    	Hometown

11:26.280 --> 11:29.580
Do gods even have blood?

11:29.840 --> 11:31.530
It's even hotter than lava.

11:31.530 --> 11:35.340
If there were even a single drop, 
this whole building would melt.

11:35.670 --> 11:37.880
That's quite the calamity...

11:38.110 --> 11:41.650
If you want to know more, make sure 
you match the "blood type" cards.

11:42.110 --> 11:44.200
Okay, now it's my turn.

11:49.400 --> 11:50.940
That posture's a bit...

11:50.940 --> 11:51.900
What's the matter?

11:52.490 --> 11:56.630
Do gods not understand the 
concept of undergarments?

11:56.630 --> 12:01.470
Yeah... I honestly don't get 
the point of underwear.

12:01.470 --> 12:05.450
Clearly, clothes already exist to cover your 
skin, so why wear anything underneath?

12:06.890 --> 12:08.910
It's making it hard for me to concentrate.

12:09.670 --> 12:12.250
Well, it wouldn't be very fair 
if you can't concentrate.

12:13.970 --> 12:16.250
Okay, I've decided. I'll take 
that one and that one.

12:20.110 --> 12:21.820
Aw, too bad.

12:20.110 --> 12:23.880
Hometown                                                                       	Name

12:21.820 --> 12:23.880
I got hometown and name so no match.

12:25.570 --> 12:29.940
Now we've seen both hometown cards, 
but do you know where they are now?

12:31.300 --> 12:34.480
The card that was revealed just now 
is currently right behind me.

12:34.670 --> 12:36.630
It's the second one from
 the back in that group of four.

12:36.630 --> 12:38.690
And the one I revealed earlier

12:38.690 --> 12:42.510
is third from the right out of the six 
cards turning by the window right now.

12:45.550 --> 12:47.480
Hometown                                    	Hometown

12:45.640 --> 12:47.490
Now, I've matched the hometown cards.

12:47.750 --> 12:48.950
Ooh!

12:49.230 --> 12:50.790
Okay, I guess I'll answer now.

12:50.790 --> 12:53.350
I think most gods share the same answer...

12:53.930 --> 12:55.890
But I'm from Elements.

12:54.560 --> 12:59.870
Elements
The Playground of the Gods

12:56.290 --> 12:59.880
It's the space you humans call 
the superior spiritual realm.

13:00.310 --> 13:01.830
It's where the gods live,

13:01.830 --> 13:05.970
so did you know that humans 
need a special door to enter there?

13:06.270 --> 13:09.400
Yes. I was using it up until six months ago.

13:10.770 --> 13:12.770
The gods are starved for games.

13:13.760 --> 13:17.730
<i>Because the gods were so bored, 
they gave humans Arises so that</i>

13:14.410 --> 13:20.010
The Seven Covenants of the Gods' Games

13:17.730 --> 13:19.660
<i>the humans could challenge them to games.</i>

13:20.680 --> 13:23.550
<i>Humans who receive an Arise from the gods will become an apostle.</i>

13:21.710 --> 13:24.230
Rule 1
Humans who receive an Arise from the gods will become an apostle

13:24.970 --> 13:29.420
<i>Humans who become apostles 
will be able to challenge the gods</i>

13:25.260 --> 13:27.480
 Arise

13:28.390 --> 13:35.400
 Rule 2
Humans who receive Arises will gain 
superhuman or magical powers and be able 
to challenge the gods to a battle of wits

13:29.420 --> 13:33.620
<i>to a battle of wits with either 
superhuman or magical powers.</i>

13:35.890 --> 13:39.670
<i>All gods' games will take place within Elements.</i>

13:36.480 --> 13:39.870
 Rule 3
 All gods' games will take place within Elements

13:40.150 --> 13:43.950
Rule 4
Arises can only be used within Elements

13:40.310 --> 13:42.720
<i>As a reward for winning a game,</i>

13:42.720 --> 13:46.590
<i>the apostle will be able to use part 
of their Arise in the real world.</i>

13:44.990 --> 13:54.550
 Rule 5
If an apostle wins in a gods' game, they will 
be able to use part of their Arises in the real world.
The more they win, the more powers 
they'll be able to use in the real world

13:47.510 --> 13:50.680
<i>Those powers are absolutely 
necessary to pioneer unexplored lands.</i>

13:51.390 --> 13:57.560
<i>Because 93% of the world 
is hostile and unexplored.</i>

14:01.290 --> 14:05.480
 Rule 6
Apostles will lose their right to play after a total of 3 losses

14:01.540 --> 14:03.070
<i>In the gods' games, an apostle</i>

14:03.070 --> 14:06.220
<i>will lose their right to play in the games 
after a total of three losses...</i>

14:05.760 --> 14:09.100
Rule 7
After winning against the gods 10 times, they will get a "Clear."

14:06.220 --> 14:08.240
<i>and will receive a "Clear" after ten victories.</i>

14:09.280 --> 14:13.240
<i>Humanity has been tasked to complete 
the game, in other words, a "Clear."</i>

14:13.920 --> 14:16.800
<i>Apostles are then given a "Celebration,"</i>

14:16.020 --> 14:21.240
Clear
By receiving 10 wins against the gods, 
the apostle will receive a "Celebration"

14:16.800 --> 14:20.000
<i>but we're still uncertain of what exactly that entails.</i>

14:21.400 --> 14:24.270
No human has pulled off this feat yet,

14:25.080 --> 14:26.300
but maybe Fay can.

14:27.730 --> 14:32.680
I'm actually slightly surprised that 
you're not hesitating to answer at all.

14:32.910 --> 14:34.310
Of course I'm not.

14:34.310 --> 14:36.240
That's just one of the rules of this game.

14:36.600 --> 14:38.600
Rules aren't meant to be mere restraints.

14:38.790 --> 14:40.200
So they're meant to be enjoyed?

14:40.650 --> 14:43.050
Correct! You're exactly right.

14:43.380 --> 14:45.520
On that note, I guess I'm up next.

14:46.590 --> 14:48.020
That one and that one.

14:51.300 --> 14:53.810
Hey, I matched the name cards.

14:52.930 --> 14:55.730
 Name

14:54.160 --> 14:55.440
So, what's your name?

14:55.740 --> 14:58.400
Oh, right. I hadn't actually 
introduced myself yet.

14:58.980 --> 15:00.250
My name is Fay Theo Philus.

15:00.580 --> 15:03.960
As you saw, Chief Secretary Miranda 
dragged me here.

15:04.390 --> 15:05.390
What's your nickname?

15:05.390 --> 15:07.390
No one's ever called me 
anything other than "Fay."

15:08.060 --> 15:11.750
I see. I guess nicknames 
count for the name card, too.

15:13.200 --> 15:16.390
<i>I guess that's something fitting 
to add on in a game of self-intros.</i>

15:16.930 --> 15:20.710
<i>What questions can you think 
up from the cards you match?</i>

15:20.980 --> 15:24.040
<i>If you're witty enough, you can stretch out the 
range of questions as much as you want.</i>

15:24.590 --> 15:25.270
<i>But...</i>

15:25.860 --> 15:28.660
<i>This isn't a game where you just pick cards.</i>

15:29.260 --> 15:32.240
<i>Even if I know where the cards are,</i>

15:32.240 --> 15:34.340
<i>not taking some cards will lead to "my" victory.</i>

15:34.980 --> 15:39.420
<i>This is an informational game where you 
have to make a selection with each turn.</i>

15:42.900 --> 15:44.760
<i>I'm starting to gather enough information...</i>

15:45.100 --> 15:47.630
<i>I'm pretty sure I know where 
the cards that I need are.</i>

15:48.040 --> 15:49.870
<i>All that's left is what she's after.</i>

15:50.290 --> 15:52.300
Next, it's my turn.

15:56.580 --> 15:57.240
Oh...

15:58.130 --> 15:59.800
<i>There's nothing written on those cards.</i>

16:00.080 --> 16:04.590
<i>Which means whoever gets those cards 
can ask whatever question they'd like.</i>

16:05.030 --> 16:07.100
<i>In a regular deck of cards, 
those would be the jokers.</i>

16:07.660 --> 16:09.960
<i>Those were one of the 
pairs I was trying to get.</i>

16:11.110 --> 16:13.000
I totally wanted these cards.

16:13.290 --> 16:16.240
Human, you remember our first promise, right?

16:16.880 --> 16:18.200
Well, yes...

16:18.580 --> 16:20.920
In that case, my question to you is...

16:23.040 --> 16:27.840
Human, what is the real reason 
you tried to get closer to me?

16:29.770 --> 16:34.180
Answer me, human. I will not allow 
any falsities to my question.

16:37.420 --> 16:39.400
<i>"Former god" my ass.</i>

16:39.630 --> 16:43.880
<i>She is very much a god!</i>

16:48.100 --> 16:51.760
<i>If you have someone to play with, 
any game is enjoyable!</i>

16:53.890 --> 16:56.350
So we both had the same motive.

16:56.820 --> 17:01.050
While we casually played the game, we 
were both actually aiming for the wild cards.

17:02.630 --> 17:04.080
But of course you were.

17:04.080 --> 17:07.540
Since that's what I was after, of course, 
a god would be after them, too.

17:09.240 --> 17:13.780
I knew a god like you would see through 
Chief Secretary Miranda's motive.

17:14.100 --> 17:17.340
But that's fine with me since 
I got to play a fun game.

17:18.320 --> 17:19.410
I'll answer you.

17:19.410 --> 17:24.520
Honestly speaking, my goal is to 
keep an eye on you, Lady Leoleshea.

17:26.090 --> 17:26.980
Wait!

17:26.980 --> 17:29.570
You're going to reduce our 
city to ashes if you tell her that!

17:30.910 --> 17:34.780
Miranda wanted to find out who you truly 
are and what your motive was.

17:36.780 --> 17:40.300
Well... I asked because 
I figured as much, but...

17:42.030 --> 17:45.880
You answered me honestly and earnestly, 
played this game with me...

17:45.880 --> 17:47.530
You are a good human.

17:47.530 --> 17:49.690
I'm not sure how to react to that...

17:50.220 --> 17:53.760
I told you from the beginning, 
didn't I? That I liked you.

17:54.070 --> 17:56.460
If I didn't, I wouldn't have bothered 
asking that question.

17:56.460 --> 17:58.850
I wouldn't ask that to 
a human I didn't trust.

18:02.400 --> 18:04.220
I'm going to call you "Fay!"

18:04.500 --> 18:06.150
You can call me "Leshea."

18:06.520 --> 18:07.750
No need to be formal with me.

18:08.140 --> 18:10.890
These games will be no fun 
if there's a distance between us.

18:10.890 --> 18:12.890
We sure didn't waste any time...

18:12.890 --> 18:14.940
Are you sure it's okay 
to be so friendly with me?

18:15.130 --> 18:18.410
Yup! You lived up to this game's potential!

18:19.290 --> 18:23.350
The cards you had gathered are 
dreams, hometown, and hobbies.

18:20.930 --> 18:22.360
 Dreams

18:22.430 --> 18:24.320
 Hometown

18:23.800 --> 18:27.330
You weren't trying to "win" against 
me in the first place, were you?

18:25.230 --> 18:27.320
Hobbies

18:27.700 --> 18:28.770
Precisely.

18:29.950 --> 18:33.660
The true nature of this game is even if 
you know where a card is, don't take it.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.860
Because this is not the same game

18:35.860 --> 18:38.180
as the original where the 
goal is to get more pairs.

18:39.410 --> 18:43.600
For example, I shouldn't take this name card.

18:43.600 --> 18:47.300
Because I already knew that your 
name is Lady Leoleshea.

18:47.310 --> 18:50.100
Since we don't get another 
turn after getting a pair,

18:50.100 --> 18:52.760
I would've just wasted my whole turn.

18:52.940 --> 18:54.520
<i>Because of the additional rule,</i>

18:54.520 --> 18:59.340
<i>you're always weighing the cards you
 memorized against the information you want.</i>

18:59.340 --> 19:01.630
<i>It's a game of information.</i>

19:02.700 --> 19:05.800
<i>Seriously... talk about a fun modification.</i>

19:06.610 --> 19:09.960
Oh, hey. I have a question for 
you, so answer me.

19:10.260 --> 19:14.010
This goes for the dreams cards, too, but you 
wanted to know what my motive was, right?

19:14.370 --> 19:18.420
What were you planning to ask me 
if you had gotten the blank cards?

19:18.760 --> 19:20.450
Would you have been so kind to answer me?

19:20.450 --> 19:23.190
Oh, right. I guess we don't need to be formal.

19:23.610 --> 19:26.340
So you're willing to answer my question?

19:26.700 --> 19:27.980
That depends on the question.

19:28.550 --> 19:32.320
Why do you stay here instead of
 returning to Elements?

19:32.690 --> 19:35.480
Also, why did you choose me?

19:35.760 --> 19:38.280
There are plenty of apostles 
more skilled than me.

19:38.720 --> 19:39.700
Because...

19:41.940 --> 19:45.570
You're the only rookie to 
get three wins in a row, right?

19:45.570 --> 19:50.460
Even in the last century, I heard that only 
a few rookies would compare to that.

19:50.460 --> 19:54.560
And, I want to Clear the 
gods' games with you.

19:54.970 --> 19:56.420
The gods' games?

19:57.020 --> 20:00.600
I came down to this realm because 
I wanted to play with the humans...

20:00.600 --> 20:05.040
But apparently it's a one way trip from 
Elements to this physical world.

20:05.680 --> 20:07.620
So I can't go back to being a god!

20:08.010 --> 20:09.100
Whoopsie!

20:09.350 --> 20:10.760
<i>Is "whoopsie" the right word to use here?!</i>

20:10.760 --> 20:14.690
It's fine. I just need to play the gods' games.

20:14.920 --> 20:16.380
Meaning...?

20:16.690 --> 20:18.990
I'm going to get ten victories in the gods' games.

20:19.310 --> 20:21.590
Then I can go back to being a god.

20:22.020 --> 20:24.280
Wait... You actually know 
what the Celebration is?

20:24.280 --> 20:26.370
The reward you get for 
winning the gods' games?

20:26.370 --> 20:30.110
Of course. It's pretty much what you humans 
have been theorizing for a while.

20:30.550 --> 20:33.310
The gods will grant you a single wish.

20:33.860 --> 20:35.790
You guys basically weren't off the mark.

20:36.180 --> 20:40.340
So it is true. But what do 
you mean by "basically"?

20:40.340 --> 20:42.300
So that's not completely true?

20:42.300 --> 20:44.420
It's not just one wish.

20:44.420 --> 20:46.750
You can have hundreds, thousands...
However many you want.

20:47.010 --> 20:49.000
Just how generous are they?!

20:49.000 --> 20:51.130
But not a single human's achieved this before.

20:51.470 --> 20:52.850
That's true...

20:53.320 --> 20:54.250
Which means...

20:55.040 --> 20:55.940
That's settled!

20:56.300 --> 20:57.000
Sorry, what?

20:57.980 --> 20:59.610
Off we go!

20:59.610 --> 21:01.560
Hey, wait! Leshea?!

21:07.020 --> 21:08.410
What are you planning to do?

21:08.650 --> 21:09.240
Huh?

21:11.900 --> 21:13.140
The Divine Gate?

21:13.530 --> 21:14.920
Wait, this is...

21:15.520 --> 21:17.870
 Ruin Branch Office of the Arcane Court Dive Center

21:15.550 --> 21:17.130
The Dive Center?

21:19.960 --> 21:22.020
I can't wait any longer!

21:22.020 --> 21:25.710
I've been waiting to find a 
human like you forever!

21:34.630 --> 21:38.460
Our gods' game is about to begin!

21:42.670 --> 21:48.730
 The Superior Spiritual Realm "???"

21:59.010 --> 22:02.550
Okay, time for Hide-and-God-Seek! 
Let the games begin!

22:02.550 --> 22:06.010
Now, hang on a second!
